&lt;p&gt;BeyondTrust is a place where you can bring your purpose to life through the work that you do, creating a safer world through our cybersecurity SaaS portfolio.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our culture of flexibility, trust, and continual learning means you will be recognized for your growth, and for the impact you make on our success. You will be surrounded by people who challenge, support, and inspire you to be the best version of yourself.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;u&gt;The Role&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for an experienced FP&amp;amp;A business partner to support our CTO and Engineering organization, as well as our CCO organization, including Professional Services, Support, Training, and Customer Success. This is a Manager-level individual contributor role spanning R&amp;amp;D investment and the direct and indirect costs of delivering and supporting our products.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our approach to FP&amp;amp;A is simple: understand what happened, determine why it matters, and help the business decide what to do next.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Cloud infrastructure economics is central to this role. We want to go significantly deeper than understanding total infrastructure spend or explaining variances. This person will partner closely with Engineering and Tech/FinOps to develop visibility into how architecture, products, customers, usage patterns, capacity, and technical decisions translate into cost and gross margin, and identify opportunities to improve those economics over time.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The role will also support productivity and operating-leverage analysis across R&amp;amp;D and the CCO organization, connecting investment and capacity to business outcomes and scalability.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;u&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Business partnering&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;CTO / Engineering / R&amp;amp;D&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a key finance partner to the CTO and Engineering organization, bringing financial and operational insight to R&amp;amp;D investment, resource allocation, productivity, and decision-making.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive deeper understanding of cloud infrastructure economics, partnering with Engineering and Tech/FinOps to connect product and customer usage, architecture, capacity, and consumption to unit economics and gross margin, and identify opportunities to improve efficiency and scalability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring a productivity lens to R&amp;amp;D investment, helping leaders understand how resources and capacity are deployed, what outcomes they support, and where operating leverage can improve.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop business cases and scenario analyses that inform investment priorities and technical and operating decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;CCO&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with CCO leadership across Professional Services, Support, Training, and Customer Success.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop a clear understanding of the operational drivers of Services margin, capacity, utilization, staffing mix, and cost to serve.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring a productivity lens across customer-facing teams, connecting resources and capacity to business and customer outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify opportunities to improve efficiency, scalability, and operating leverage while balancing customer needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;FP&amp;amp;A &amp;amp; performance management&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the budget, forecast, and performance outlook across the supported organizations, ensuring Finance has a clear and reliable view of results, risks, and opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Connect business activity and operational drivers to financial outcomes, including gross margin, cost to serve, and R&amp;amp;D investment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to product P&amp;amp;Ls and product-level profitability views by connecting R&amp;amp;D investment, infrastructure costs, and customer-delivery costs to product economics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring insights from the business back into the broader FP&amp;amp;A organization, helping inform company-level forecasts, planning, and management reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Explain performance drivers, assess their implications, and recommend appropriate actions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continuously improve models, data, and processes so more time can be spent on analysis and decision&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;u&gt;What You’ll Bring&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated, hands-on depth in SaaS cloud infrastructure economics, including consumption drivers, unit economics, scalability, and gross-margin implications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Approximately 5–8+ years of progressive experience in FP&amp;amp;A, strategic finance, finance analytics, FinOps, or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in a $300M–$1B PE-backed or pre-IPO enterprise B2B SaaS company, or a highly comparable environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience partnering with Engineering, Technology, Product, or Tech/FinOps leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of SaaS gross margin and cost-to-serve economics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional financial modeling and analytical skills, including the ability to work through complex or imperfect operational data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to independently move from analysis to insight to a clear point of view and recommendation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical curiosity and enough fluency to engage credibly with Engineering and keep digging beyond the first explanation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication and influencing skills, with the ability to work effectively with senior leaders in an individual contributor capacity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;u&gt;Better Together&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Diversity. Inclusion. They’re more than just words for us. They are the guiding values of how we build our teams, cultivate leaders, and create a culture where people feel connected.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We take care of our employees so they can take care of our customers. Customers who&amp;nbsp;come from all walks of life just like us. We hire incredible people from diverse backgrounds because when we are different together, we are stronger together.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;u&gt;About Us&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;BeyondTrust is the global identity security leader protecting Paths to Privilege™. Our identity-centric approach goes beyond securing privileges and access, empowering organizations with the most effective solution to manage the entire identity attack surface and neutralize threats, whether from external attacks or insiders.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;BeyondTrust is leading the charge in transforming identity security to prevent breaches and limit the blast radius of attacks, while creating a superior customer experience and operational efficiencies. We are trusted by 20,000 customers, including 75 of the Fortune 100, and our global ecosystem of partners.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Learn more at &lt;a href=&quot;http://www.beyondtrust.com/&quot;&gt;www.beyondtrust.com&lt;/a&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
